      "dcterms:title": "Verified computations for closed hyperbolic 3-manifolds",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Goerner, Matthias"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20210107",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.12095",
      "dcterms:abstract": "Extending methods ﬁrst used by Casson, we show how to verify a hyper- bolic structure on a ﬁnite triangulation of a closed 3-manifold using interval arith- metic methods. A key ingredient is a new theoretical result (akin to a theorem by Neumann-Zagier and Moser for ideal triangulations upon which HIKMOT is based) showing that there is a redundancy among the edge equations if the edges avoid “gim- bal lock”. We successfully test the algorithm on known examples such as the ori- entable closed manifolds in the Hodgson-Weeks census and the bundle census by Bell. We also tackle a previously unsolved problem and determine all knots and links with up to 14 crossings that have a hyperbolic branched double cover.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-1904.12095v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-1904.12095v2"
    }
  ]
